    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0557" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg515"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 23, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 21st instant, accompanied by a copy of a letter
                    addressed to you by Mr. J. M. Vernon, who claims to be a British subject, who
                    was rescued from the steamer Huntress, a blockade-runner from Charleston, and
                    subsequently committed to Fort Lafayette.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to acquaint you that the case shall forthwith be
                    examined, with a view to such further proceedings as the result may appear to
                    call for.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
